This license covers this repository's own code (disassemblers, analysis
scripts, memory-map tooling) and written analysis/documentation only.

**It does not cover, and does not grant any rights to, Atari 2600 game ROM
images.** Atari 2600 ROMs are, in general, still under copyright. This
project does not host, bulk-distribute, or commit copyrighted ROM binaries
to this repository under any circumstance. Analysis targets are limited to:
(a) ROMs in the public domain or released under an explicit open license by
their rights holder (e.g. published homebrew with a stated open license),
(b) ROM files the user has supplied from their own legally obtained copies,
used only for local analysis and never redistributed here, or (c)
commentary/disassembly of material already extensively documented in the
public reverse-engineering literature (the Stella project, 6502.org,
AtariAge's development forums), cited rather than reproduced wholesale. See
`data/README.md` and `config/claude.md` for the standing rule this repeats
on every session start.
